A friend and I did the same thing in wizard(debug mode) a number of times,
then we looked at the source code, and now we believe we understand
the difference between anger and alignment, and how to successfully
convert yourself every time, without having to kill and carry a unicorn
of your current alignment, or finding a helm of opposite alignment:

What we've discovered is that anger has nothing to do with it.  Your god
can fry you to a crisp, and you still will convert the alter rather than
yourself.  Also, LUCK plays no part either.  You must change how aligned
you are with your current god in order to change.  You need to go from
"You are stridently aligned" levels of alignment to a "You have strayed"
alignment.

Method 1)  Kill a peaceful monster.  If you throw something at a
monster to attack it, and it gets angry, your alignment will NOT
be affected.  You must attack it by hitting.  A corollary is you can
get rid of the pesky peaceful creature hanging out with you at the
alter without hurting your relationship with your god by throwing something
at the monster to make it angry or to kill it outright.

Once you've killed a peaceful monster by responding "y" to a "really attack"
prompt, you can then offer a fresh corpse to the alter of other alignment
and the new god will "accept your allegience."

Method 2) Donate $400 * your current experience level to a priest of the
alignment you wish to convert to.  Then offer on the alter.  Very convenient.
The alter is right there.  Be careful with this.  It appears that
donating TOO much gold doesn't do anything for you.  You may also have
to donate more than once to "stray" sufficiently.  Method 1 may be a
more sure methodology.
